    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-special-residence-requirements-act-2013-sch-1-sec-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4 At the end of section 22A",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-amendment-special-residence-requirements-act-2013#sch-1-sec-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-citizenship-amendment-special-residence-requirements-act-2013.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-citizenship-amendment-special-residence-requirements-act-2013.pdf, p.8",
      "values:originalText": "Add:\nRules relating to power under subsection (1A)\n\n(6) The power under subsection (1A) may only be exercised by the\nMinister personally.\n\n(7) The Minister does not have a duty to consider whether to exercise\nthe power under subsection (1A), whether he or she is requested to\ndo so by the applicant or by any other person, or in any other\ncircumstances.\n\n(8) The Minister may, by writing, approve a form for the purposes of\nparagraph (1A)(e).\n\n(9) If the applicant becomes an Australian citizen in circumstances\nwhere the Minister exercised the power under subsection (1A), the\nMinister must cause to be tabled in each House of the Parliament,\nwithin 15 sitting days of that House after the day the applicant\nbecomes an Australian citizen, a statement that:\n\n(a) states that the Minister has exercised the power under\nsubsection (1A); and\n\n(b) states the activity covered by paragraph (1)(a); and\n\n(c) sets out the reasons for the Minister’s exercise of that power,\nincluding why the Minister considers that engagement in that\nactivity would be of benefit to Australia.\n\n(10) However, a statement under subsection (9) is not to include the\nname of the applicant.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2013A00057\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\n\n(11) A determination under subsection (1A) is not a legislative\ninstrument.",
      "skos:definition": "Add:\nRules relating to power under subsection (1A)\n\n(6) The power under subsection (1A) may only be exercised by the\nMinister personally.\n\n(7) The Minister does not have a duty to consider whether to exercise\nthe power under subsection (1A), whether he or she is requested to\ndo so by the applicant or by any other person, or in any other\ncircumstances.\n\n(8) The Minister may, by writing, approve a form for the purposes of\nparagraph (1A)(e).\n\n(9) If the applicant becomes an Australian citizen in circumstances\nwhere the Minister exercised the power under subsection (1A), the\nMinister must cause to be tabled in each House of the Parliament,\nwithin 15 sitting days of that House after the day the applicant\nbecomes an Australian citizen, a statement that:\n\n(a) states that the Minister has exercised the power under\nsubsection (1A); and\n\n(b) states the activity covered by paragraph (1)(a); and\n\n(c) sets out the reasons for the Minister’s exercise of that power,\nincluding why the Minister considers that engagement in that\nactivity would be of benefit to Australia.\n\n(10) However, a statement under subsection (9) is not to include the\nname of the applicant.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2013A00057\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\n\n(11) A determination under subsection (1A) is not a legislative\ninstrument.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-special-residence-requirements-act-2013-sch-1-sec-4-ss-6"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-special-residence-requirements-act-2013-sch-1-sec-4-ss-7"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-special-residence-requirements-act-2013-sch-1-sec-4-ss-8"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-special-residence-requirements-act-2013-sch-1-sec-4-ss-9"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-special-residence-requirements-act-2013-sch-1-sec-4-ss-10"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-special-residence-requirements-act-2013-sch-1-sec-4-ss-11"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f2f99736d9155a1b90827ce08ec0e2c54ae9d335d0bc91677eaec224f02be8d6"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-amendment-special-residence-requirements-act-2013#sch-1-sec-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4 At the end of section 22A",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 8,
      "values:originalText": "Add:\nRules relating to power under subsection (1A)\n\n(6) The power under subsection (1A) may only be exercised by the\nMinister personally.\n\n(7) The Minister does not have a duty to consider whether to exercise\nthe power under subsection (1A), whether he or she is requested to\ndo so by the applicant or by any other person, or in any other\ncircumstances.\n\n(8) The Minister may, by writing, approve a form for the purposes of\nparagraph (1A)(e).\n\n(9) If the applicant becomes an Australian citizen in circumstances\nwhere the Minister exercised the power under subsection (1A), the\nMinister must cause to be tabled in each House of the Parliament,\nwithin 15 sitting days of that House after the day the applicant\nbecomes an Australian citizen, a statement that:\n\n(a) states that the Minister has exercised the power under\nsubsection (1A); and\n\n(b) states the activity covered by paragraph (1)(a); and\n\n(c) sets out the reasons for the Minister’s exercise of that power,\nincluding why the Minister considers that engagement in that\nactivity would be of benefit to Australia.\n\n(10) However, a statement under subsection (9) is not to include the\nname of the applicant.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2013A00057\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\n\n(11) A determination under subsection (1A) is not a legislative\ninstrument."
    },
