    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-special-residence-requirements-act-2013-sch-1-sec-4-ss-9",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4(9) At the end of section 22A",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-amendment-special-residence-requirements-act-2013#sch-1-sec-4-ss-9"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-citizenship-amendment-special-residence-requirements-act-2013.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-citizenship-amendment-special-residence-requirements-act-2013.pdf, p.8",
      "values:originalText": "(9) If the applicant becomes an Australian citizen in circumstances\nwhere the Minister exercised the power under subsection (1A), the\nMinister must cause to be tabled in each House of the Parliament,\nwithin 15 sitting days of that House after the day the applicant\nbecomes an Australian citizen, a statement that:\n\n(a) states that the Minister has exercised the power under\nsubsection (1A); and\n\n(b) states the activity covered by paragraph (1)(a); and\n\n(c) sets out the reasons for the Minister’s exercise of that power,\nincluding why the Minister considers that engagement in that\nactivity would be of benefit to Australia.",
      "skos:definition": "(9) If the applicant becomes an Australian citizen in circumstances\nwhere the Minister exercised the power under subsection (1A), the\nMinister must cause to be tabled in each House of the Parliament,\nwithin 15 sitting days of that House after the day the applicant\nbecomes an Australian citizen, a statement that:\n\n(a) states that the Minister has exercised the power under\nsubsection (1A); and\n\n(b) states the activity covered by paragraph (1)(a); and\n\n(c) sets out the reasons for the Minister’s exercise of that power,\nincluding why the Minister considers that engagement in that\nactivity would be of benefit to Australia.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-special-residence-requirements-act-2013-sch-1-sec-4"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-special-residence-requirements-act-2013-sch-1-sec-4-ss-9-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-special-residence-requirements-act-2013-sch-1-sec-4-ss-9-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "540b8f6091ace1f808a615a1926b2def12185d6d475567628fd47a72658f0d12",
      "skos:note": "Minister must provide statement to Parliament after applicant becomes Australian citizen.",
      "dc:description": "Yes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-amendment-special-residence-requirements-act-2013#sch-1-sec-4-ss-9",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4(9) At the end of section 22A",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 8,
      "values:originalText": "(9) If the applicant becomes an Australian citizen in circumstances\nwhere the Minister exercised the power under subsection (1A), the\nMinister must cause to be tabled in each House of the Parliament,\nwithin 15 sitting days of that House after the day the applicant\nbecomes an Australian citizen, a statement that:\n\n(a) states that the Minister has exercised the power under\nsubsection (1A); and\n\n(b) states the activity covered by paragraph (1)(a); and\n\n(c) sets out the reasons for the Minister’s exercise of that power,\nincluding why the Minister considers that engagement in that\nactivity would be of benefit to Australia."
    },
