    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-special-residence-requirements-act-2013-sch-1-sec-9-ss-9",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "9(9) At the end of section 22B",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-amendment-special-residence-requirements-act-2013#sch-1-sec-9-ss-9"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-citizenship-amendment-special-residence-requirements-act-2013.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-citizenship-amendment-special-residence-requirements-act-2013.pdf, p.10",
      "values:originalText": "(9) If the person becomes an Australian citizen in circumstances where\nthe Minister exercised the power under subsection (1A), the\nMinister must cause to be tabled in each House of the Parliament,\nwithin 15 sitting days of that House after the day the person\nbecomes an Australian citizen, a statement that:\n\n(a) states that the Minister has exercised the power under\nsubsection (1A); and\n\n(b) states the kind of work covered by paragraph (1)(a); and\n\n(c) sets out the reasons for the Minister’s exercise of that power,\nincluding why the Minister considers that engagement in that\nkind of work is of benefit to Australia.",
      "skos:definition": "(9) If the person becomes an Australian citizen in circumstances where\nthe Minister exercised the power under subsection (1A), the\nMinister must cause to be tabled in each House of the Parliament,\nwithin 15 sitting days of that House after the day the person\nbecomes an Australian citizen, a statement that:\n\n(a) states that the Minister has exercised the power under\nsubsection (1A); and\n\n(b) states the kind of work covered by paragraph (1)(a); and\n\n(c) sets out the reasons for the Minister’s exercise of that power,\nincluding why the Minister considers that engagement in that\nkind of work is of benefit to Australia.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-special-residence-requirements-act-2013-sch-1-sec-9"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-special-residence-requirements-act-2013-sch-1-sec-9-ss-9-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-special-residence-requirements-act-2013-sch-1-sec-9-ss-9-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-special-residence-requirements-act-2013-sch-1-sec-9-ss-9-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "54b326315aa0e365d7fe9f37d1f44dd0ffc05c88e49528306f0799f72b0d40aa",
      "skos:note": "Minister must provide statement to Parliament after granting citizenship in certain circumstances.",
      "dc:description": "Yes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-amendment-special-residence-requirements-act-2013#sch-1-sec-9-ss-9",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "9(9) At the end of section 22B",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 10,
      "values:originalText": "(9) If the person becomes an Australian citizen in circumstances where\nthe Minister exercised the power under subsection (1A), the\nMinister must cause to be tabled in each House of the Parliament,\nwithin 15 sitting days of that House after the day the person\nbecomes an Australian citizen, a statement that:\n\n(a) states that the Minister has exercised the power under\nsubsection (1A); and\n\n(b) states the kind of work covered by paragraph (1)(a); and\n\n(c) sets out the reasons for the Minister’s exercise of that power,\nincluding why the Minister considers that engagement in that\nkind of work is of benefit to Australia."
    },
